            "description": "Many of our backwater towns in over a dozen of our states do not even have the technology to agriculturally produce. They are still stuck in the Gilded Age while the rest of the country moves drastically forward. It is no wonder that they cannot make what the rest of the country requires them to make. I will give all of our farmers better technology, so they won’t be behind when the time comes to supply our nation."
        }
    },
    {
        "model": "campaign_trail.answer",
        "pk": 49080,
        "fields": {
            "question": 48024,
            "description": "I think, with some of the New Deal provisions even rolled back during Roosevelt’s term, and the war’s conclusion, that the farmers will be able to compete in a way they never have before. The market has rebounded quite a bit thanks to the increase in demand. The farmers of the country should have no problem with their production once we reduce any remaining wartime controls on our economy."
        }
    },
    {
        "model": "campaign_trail.answer",
        "pk": 49081,
        "fields": {
            "question": 48024,
            "description": "Neither Dewey’s approach of a hands-off agricultural economy nor Franklin Roosevelt’s endless subsidies are the solution to this issue. We can put all of these rogue agencies supporting various things for farmers into one overarching agricultural program, combining them all into one coherent thing that can assist the farmers of America in times of severe decline."
        }
    },
    {
        "model": "campaign_trail.answer",
        "pk": 49082,
        "fields": {
            "question": 48025,
            "description": "I think this would be a great idea. Let’s make sure Dewey and I are put in the same room, and we will spar with our words. I will be as respectful as possible around the man, and hope for a good, hearty discussion between the two of us. I can only hope Americans will see the debate the same way as the President and I do."
        }
    },
    {
        "model": "campaign_trail.answer",
        "pk": 49083,
        "fields": {
            "question": 48025,
            "description": "No, no, I cannot. To go out there on a stage such as that and possibly make a fool of myself, with the election this close, would be a rash and stupid decision. What I will do instead is continue to zip across the nation, giving as many speeches as we can while Dewey awaits our response to his challenge. A debate sounds like a novel idea, but this is just not the time."
