    },
    {
        "model": "campaign_trail.answer",
        "pk": 49084,
        "fields": {
            "question": 48025,
            "description": "Why don’t we turn back the clock a little bit, so to speak? Lincoln and Douglas were able to do it a hundred years ago, and they still gained national news. I’d like to debate the President truly in person, out of doors, in front of a crowd of hundreds. If the President doesn’t want to debate me then, then he is not really looking for a true debate. He just wants to boost his numbers."
        }
    },
    {
        "model": "campaign_trail.answer",
        "pk": 49085,
        "fields": {
            "question": 48026,
            "description": "Thomas Dewey is a good man, but what he has done to destroy every aspect of the New Deal is unforgivable. Franklin Roosevelt saved millions of lives from certain doom, and the idea of rolling those very same policies back should be frightening to anyone. I will continue that tradition in the White House, and keep the presidency in the possession of the people."
