            "description": "I will make one last call to all men in organized labor in this country. I may not be who you wanted to be your Democratic candidate for president, but you must see the detriment you will face by electing Dewey. Not voting for me is a vote for Dewey, and he will enjoy the White House for four more years, suppressing you all even more and making more money for him and his New York cronies."
        }
    },
    {
        "model": "campaign_trail.answer",
        "pk": 49087,
        "fields": {
            "question": 48026,
            "description": "I know President Dewey has made remarkable moves overseas, and that is wonderful. However, I will also have everyone in America know that my foreign accomplishments far outweighed his before he entered his office, and yet I am still the one portrayed as the ill-informed one in this race. It is time we dispelled that."
        }
    },
    {
        "model": "campaign_trail.answer",
        "pk": 49088,
        "fields": {
            "question": 48026,
            "description": "It's fairly simple, in my opinion. Dewey is from the party of Hoover, business and depression. I represent the party of FDR, the worker, the laborer, the farmer. If you cannot see through this simple construction of our current election, you must now, lest Hoover’s men stay in power once again."
