            "question": 48027,
            "description": "Oh… wow. Well, I was operating under the idea that Dillinger was an innocent man, targeted by a corrupt Chicago Police Force. He was considered a folk hero back when I did this; I was only trying to do what I thought was right at the time, and he was eventually killed anyway, which was marked as “justifiable homicide.” I don’t think any homicide is justifiable, and neither is this attack from the President on an event that transpired over a decade ago."
